{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"misogynic-scheelite-solitaire","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\n\nA gate (`review-plan`, `verify-completion`) reads its `[tool.rebar.llm]` model config from the attested snapshot root (`origin/main`), by design since bug 2876 (`src/rebar/llm/config_readers.py:46-56`), but executes the locally installed rebar code. When `main` changes models in a way that needs matching code, every worktree still on the older code fails its gates.\n\nObserved 2026-11-09 19:32 PST: commit `06b3b1a5230` (\"Move configured models to the 5.5 generation\") moved the config to `bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-5-5` and, in the same commit, added the `_MODEL_ID_CAPABILITY_OVERRIDES` rows that stop sending `temperature` to 5.5 models. `rebar review-plan maize-guilty-hapuku`, run from a worktree at `49f5d6d0580` (the parent of `06b3b1a5230`), returned `INDETERMINATE` with `llm_ran: false`: Bedrock rejected `temperature` with a 400 ValidationException. The same review after `git merge --ff-only origin/main` plus `make install` ran the model normally (19:42 PST).\n\nEffects:\n- The verdict is an unsigned `INDETERMINATE` with no finding naming the cause; the reason is only in `coverage.llm_error`.\n- That error suggests editing `_MODEL_ID_CAPABILITY_OVERRIDES` or unsetting temperature, though the fix already exists on `main` and the real remedy is updating the local install.\n\n## Expected\n\nA gate run whose attested config is newer than the executing code either detects the skew and says so (naming the attested SHA, the local code version, and the remedy: update the worktree and `make install`), or resolves model capabilities consistently with the config it read.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A gate run whose attested `[tool.rebar.llm]` config names a model the local code cannot drive reports the version skew and the update remedy, instead of only a provider 400 in `coverage.llm_error`; pinned by a test that pairs a newer attested config with older capability tables.","id":"ac3b-c6cd-8076-4a98","parent_id":"","priority":3,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Gates read model config from origin/main but run local code, so stale worktrees fail"},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1794282292997487001,"uuid":"329e8835-f3c0-4538-be19-52cd536919ae"}